                "blankWaterplaneSquareMetres": "The five square logs as they lie, 5 m by 1 m at any draft",
                "unhewnLitres": "The square 1 m trunk of five logs, 5000 L, less the finished hull's 1671 L envelope (bin/lib/hulls/dugout.py): hewn away a sixth at each hewing, as the outside is shaped. Shaping it is not timed: the strokes that hew out the char shape the outside with them, a simplification for play until shaping gets work of its own",
                "clay": "Wet clay one voxel thick over the rim outline the shape draws (its Clay group), at vanilla's 25 voxels a ball (BEClayForm.PutClay)",
                "axeEdgeMetres": "Char has lost its fibres and crumbles, so a stroke breaks it away down to the sound wood along its whole sweep across the hollow, a strip as wide as the axe's edge, about 10 cm on a felling axe",
                "hollowBeamMetres": "The hollow's width the stroke sweeps: the hull's 0.9 m beam less its two 5 cm walls (bin/lib/hulls/dugout.py)",
                "wallMetres": "Her shell's 5 cm walls: a fire burning with the rim unguarded chars it at the hollow's rate, and once the char reaches through a wall's thickness the blank is spoiled",
                "secondsPerStroke": "The best working rhythm with an axe is 25 to 35 strokes a minute (H. Glaser, physiology of forestry work, FAO)",
                "hewSaturation": "As hard as a patch of mending: hewing out a day's char by hand"
